<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE topic
        SYSTEM "https://resources.jetbrains.com/writerside/1.0/xhtml-entities.dtd">
<topic xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
       xsi:noNamespaceSchemaLocation="https://resources.jetbrains.com/writerside/1.0/topic.v2.xsd"
       title="Kotlinmailer Modules" id="modules">

    <title>
        Kotlinmailer Modules
    </title>
    <chapter title="Dependencies" id="dependencies">
        <p>Kotlinmailer modules are available from Maven Central repository. To use them you have to add appropriate
            dependency into your repositories mapping.</p>
        <tabs group="build">
            <tab title="Kotlin Gradle" group-key="build-gradle-kotlin">
                <code-block lang="kotlin">
                    repositories {
                        mavenCentral()
                    }
                </code-block>
            </tab>
            <tab title="Groovy Gradle" group-key="build-gradle-groovy">
                <code-block lang="groovy">
                    repositories {
                        mavenCentral()
                    }
                </code-block>
            </tab>
            <tab title="Maven" group-key="build-maven">
                The Maven Central repository is enabled by default for Maven users.
            </tab>
        </tabs>

    </chapter>
    <chapter title="Base Modules" id="base-modules">
        Kotlinmailer is split into multiple modules so that you can select only those dependencies you need and thereby
        eliminate unnecessary peer dependencies. The <code>core</code> module is required for all other modules to work.

        <list>
            <li>
                <control><code>core</code></control>
                <control>(required)</control>
                the email model, builder DSL and MIME renderer.
            </li>
            <li>
                <control><code>smtp</code></control>
                to send emails via SMTP. You can find more information <a href="mailer.md">here</a>.
            </li>
            <li>
                <control><code>jmap</code></control>
                to send emails via JMAP. It needs a <a href="https://ktor.io/docs/client-engines.html">Ktor client
                engine</a>.
            </li>
            <li>
                <control><code>html</code></control>
                if you want to use kotlinx.html inside your email builders.
                You can find more information <a href="html.md">here</a>.
            </li>
        </list>

        <table>
            <tr>
                <td>Module</td>
                <td>Platforms</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td><code>core</code>, <code>html</code>, <code>jmap</code></td>
                <td>JVM, JS, Wasm, macOS, iOS, Linux, Windows</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td><code>smtp</code></td>
                <td>JVM (incl. Android), JS (Node.js only), macOS, iOS, Linux and Windows (without TLS)</td>
            </tr>
        </table>

        <warning>
            Since version 1.0.1, the module names have changed.
            Before modules were prefixed with <code>kotlinmailer-</code> as for example <code>kotlinmailer-core</code>. These modules are deprecated but unfortunately, can't be removed from maven central due to sonatype's policy.
        </warning>

        <tabs group="build">
            <tab title="Kotlin Gradle" group-key="build-gradle-kotlin">
                <code-block lang="kotlin">
                    val kotlinmailer_version = "%kotlinmailer_version%"
                    dependencies {
                        implementation("at.quickme.kotlinmailer:core:$kotlinmailer_version")
                        implementation("at.quickme.kotlinmailer:smtp:$kotlinmailer_version")
                        // optional
                        implementation("at.quickme.kotlinmailer:jmap:$kotlinmailer_version")
                        implementation("at.quickme.kotlinmailer:html:$kotlinmailer_version")
                    }
                </code-block>
                In Kotlin Multiplatform projects, add the dependencies to <code>commonMain</code>.
                Alternatively, if you use gradle version catalogues you can use the following:
                <code-block lang="text">
                    [versions]
                    //...
                    kotlinmailer = "%kotlinmailer_version%"

                    [libraries]
                    //...
                    kotlinmailer-core = { module = "at.quickme.kotlinmailer:core", version.ref = "kotlinmailer" }
                    kotlinmailer-smtp = { module = "at.quickme.kotlinmailer:smtp", version.ref = "kotlinmailer" }
                    // optional
                    kotlinmailer-jmap = { module = "at.quickme.kotlinmailer:jmap", version.ref = "kotlinmailer" }
                    kotlinmailer-html = { module = "at.quickme.kotlinmailer:html", version.ref = "kotlinmailer" }
                </code-block>
                And then in your dependencies block:
                <code-block lang="kotlin">
                    dependencies {
                        implementation(libs.kotlinmailer.core)
                        implementation(libs.kotlinmailer.smtp)
                        // optional
                        implementation(libs.kotlinmailer.jmap)
                        implementation(libs.kotlinmailer.html)
                    }
                </code-block>
            </tab>
            <tab title="Groovy Gradle" group-key="build-gradle-groovy">
                <code-block lang="groovy">
                    def kotlinmailer_version = "%kotlinmailer_version%"
                    dependencies {
                        implementation "at.quickme.kotlinmailer:core:$kotlinmailer_version"
                        implementation "at.quickme.kotlinmailer:smtp:$kotlinmailer_version"
                        // optional
                        implementation "at.quickme.kotlinmailer:jmap:$kotlinmailer_version"
                        implementation "at.quickme.kotlinmailer:html:$kotlinmailer_version"
                    }
                </code-block>
            </tab>
            <tab title="Maven" group-key="build-maven">
                <code-block lang="xml">
                    <![CDATA[
                     <dependencies>
                         <dependency>
                             <groupId>at.quickme.kotlinmailer</groupId>
                             <artifactId>core-jvm</artifactId>
                             <version>%kotlinmailer_version%</version>
                         </dependency>
                         <dependency>
                             <groupId>at.quickme.kotlinmailer</groupId>
                             <artifactId>smtp-jvm</artifactId>
                             <version>%kotlinmailer_version%</version>
                         </dependency>
                         <!-- optional html -->
                         <dependency>
                             <groupId>at.quickme.kotlinmailer</groupId>
                             <artifactId>html-jvm</artifactId>
                             <version>%kotlinmailer_version%</version>
                         </dependency>
                     </dependencies>
                    ]]>
                </code-block>
            </tab>
        </tabs>
    </chapter>

</topic>
